    {
      "id": "tiktok-7709970947318762755",
      "number": 6,
      "title": "The fast start isn't the win. Finishing is. You've done this before: two weeks of going all in, every night, every weekend. Then one bad week and you can't even look at it. Obsession feels like progress because it's loud. But it runs on adrenaline, and adrenaline runs out. Discipline is quieter. It just shows up again tomorrow at the same pace. So pick a pace you could keep on your worst day, not your best one. Twenty minutes. One page. One rep. Then stop, even if you want more. Same stairs. One step at a time.",
      "caption": "The fast start isn't the win. Finishing is. You've done this before: two weeks of going all in, every night, every weekend. Then one bad week and you can't even look at it. Obsession feels like progress because it's loud. But it runs on adrenaline, and adrenaline runs out. Discipline is quieter. It just shows up again tomorrow at the same pace. So pick a pace you could keep on your worst day, not your best one. Twenty minutes. One page. One rep. Then stop, even if you want more. Same stairs. One step at a time.",
